  {
    "name": "RTP with padding: the last byte is a count, not payload",
    "input": {
      "packet": "a008000700001f40010203041122000003",
      "view": "fields"
    },
    "match": "subset",
    "why": "the load-bearing assertion is that the payload is 2 bytes and not 5. A decoder that ignores the padding count reports three padding bytes as data and looks right",
    "fieldCount": 9,
    "expect": {
      "kind": "fields",
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "V / P / X / CC",
          "value": "2 / 1 / 0 / 0"
        },
        {
          "label": "Padding",
          "value": "3 bytes",
          "tone": "warn"
        },
        {
          "label": "Payload",
          "value": "2 bytes",
          "note": "not decoded; the payload type says how"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "a compound RTCP packet: SR with a report block, then SDES with a CNAME",
    "input": {
      "packet": "81c8000c11111111e8754700499602d20036ee8000001388000c3500222222221a000005000005dc00000028aabbccdd0000303981ca0006111111110111616c696365406578616d706c652e636f6d00",
      "view": "fields"
    },
    "match": "subset",
    "why": "pins the compound walk: finding the second sub-packet at all depends on reading the length field as words-minus-one, which is the classic RTCP off-by-one",
    "fieldCount": 16,
    "expect": {
      "kind": "fields",
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Protocol",
          "value": "RTCP"
        },
        {
          "label": "Sub-packets",
